---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Block-causal mask matrix: 12 positions = 3 blocks of 4.
// Cell (q, k) is visible when block(k) <= block(q); within-block is bidirectional.
const N = 12;
const BLK = 4;
const maskRows = Array.from({ length: N }, (_, q) => ({
  q,
  cells: Array.from({ length: N }, (_, k) => {
    const bq = Math.floor(q / BLK);
    const bk = Math.floor(k / BLK);
    return { k, cls: bk < bq ? 'm-past' : bk === bq ? 'm-intra' : 'm-off' };
  }),
}));
---

<Base
  title="SDAR block-diffusion anatomy — Junwon Lee"
  description="Interactive anatomy of an SDAR-style block-diffusion language model: the transformer stack, block-causal attention, and confidence-based parallel decoding with an exact, append-only KV cache."
>
  <div class="sdar-page">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Study · Model anatomy</p>
        <h1>Inside SDAR: a block-diffusion LM, tensor by tensor</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          SDAR-style models keep the ordinary decoder transformer — same weights, same shapes —
          and change only how it reads and writes text: autoregressive <em>across</em> blocks,
          parallel diffusion-denoising <em>inside</em> each block (블록 단위로). Walk the stack,
          open a layer, then step through decoding and watch the KV cache grow.
        </p>

        <div class="jump-row">
          <a class="tag" href="#stack-view">1 · Model stack</a>
          <a class="tag" href="#layer-view">2 · Layer internals</a>
          <a class="tag" href="#decode-view">3 · Decoding timeline</a>
        </div>

        <div class="config-note">
          <span class="config-lead">Config assumed on this page — the public SDAR-1.7B setup
          (a Qwen3-1.7B backbone adapted to block diffusion):</span>
          <span class="tag accent">d_model 2,048</span>
          <span class="tag">28 layers</span>
          <span class="tag">16 Q heads / 8 KV heads (GQA)</span>
          <span class="tag">head_dim 128</span>
          <span class="tag">FFN 6,144 (SwiGLU)</span>
          <span class="tag">vocab 151,936</span>
          <span class="tag accent">block length 4</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 1 · MODEL STACK ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="stack-view">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h">1 · The model stack</h2>
        <p class="viz-sub">Hover any box for exact parameter counts and bytes. Click a
          transformer block to open its internals.</p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <div class="sdar-scroll">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 740 640" role="img" aria-label="SDAR model stack: tokens, embedding, 28 transformer blocks, LM head, block-diffusion decoding loop" style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:720px;">
            <defs>
              <marker id="arrS" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#87857c"></path>
              </marker>
              <marker id="arrSa" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#c15f3c"></path>
              </marker>
            </defs>

            <!-- input tokens -->
            <g data-tip="At decode time the sequence is: committed tokens (clean) + the active block's [MASK] placeholders. Length L integers, one id per position.">
              <rect class="sbox" x="120" y="14" width="320" height="48" rx="10"></rect>
              <text class="stitle" x="280" y="34" text-anchor="middle">input token ids — [L]</text>
              <text class="ssub" x="280" y="52" text-anchor="middle">“The capital of France is” + 4 × [MASK]</text>
            </g>
            <line class="flowline" x1="280" y1="62" x2="280" y2="76" marker-end="url(#arrS)"></line>

            <!-- embedding -->
            <g data-tip="Lookup: each id selects a 2,048-dim row. 151,936 × 2,048 = 311,164,928 params ≈ 622 MB in BF16. Tied: the same matrix is reused (transposed) as the LM head.">
              <rect class="sbox" x="120" y="78" width="320" height="56" rx="10"></rect>
              <text class="stitle" x="280" y="100" text-anchor="middle">token embedding E</text>
              <text class="smono" x="280" y="122" text-anchor="middle">[151,936 × 2,048] · 311.2 M params · tied with LM head</text>
            </g>
            <line class="flowline" x1="280" y1="134" x2="280" y2="148" marker-end="url(#arrS)"></line>

            <!-- transformer blocks -->
            <a href="#layer-view" class="blk-link" aria-label="Open transformer block internals">
              <g class="clickable" data-tip="Per layer: Q 4.19 M + K 2.10 M + V 2.10 M + O 4.19 M + SwiGLU MLP 37.75 M + norms ≈ 50.33 M params ≈ 100.7 MB BF16. Click to open.">
                <rect class="sbox sbox-blk" x="120" y="150" width="320" height="56" rx="10"></rect>
                <text class="stitle" x="280" y="172" text-anchor="middle">transformer block 1</text>
                <text class="ssub" x="280" y="192" text-anchor="middle">attn 12.58 M · MLP 37.75 M · click to open ↓</text>
              </g>
            </a>
            <line class="flowline-thin" x1="280" y1="206" x2="280" y2="216"></line>
            <a href="#layer-view" class="blk-link" aria-label="Open transformer block internals">
              <g class="clickable" data-tip="Identical shape every layer. Only the weights differ.">
                <rect class="sbox sbox-blk" x="120" y="216" width="320" height="56" rx="10"></rect>
                <text class="stitle" x="280" y="238" text-anchor="middle">transformer block 2</text>
                <text class="ssub" x="280" y="258" text-anchor="middle">attn 12.58 M · MLP 37.75 M</text>
              </g>
            </a>
            <line class="flowline-dash" x1="280" y1="272" x2="280" y2="316"></line>
            <rect x="164" y="284" width="232" height="20" fill="#ffffff"></rect>
            <text class="ssub" x="280" y="298" text-anchor="middle">⋯ blocks 3 – 27 (24 more, identical) ⋯</text>
            <a href="#layer-view" class="blk-link" aria-label="Open transformer block internals">
              <g class="clickable" data-tip="28 layers total: 28 × 50.33 M = 1,409 M backbone params ≈ 2.82 GB BF16.">
                <rect class="sbox sbox-blk" x="120" y="316" width="320" height="56" rx="10"></rect>
                <text class="stitle" x="280" y="338" text-anchor="middle">transformer block 28</text>
                <text class="ssub" x="280" y="358" text-anchor="middle">attn 12.58 M · MLP 37.75 M</text>
              </g>
            </a>
            <line class="flowline" x1="280" y1="372" x2="280" y2="388" marker-end="url(#arrS)"></line>

            <!-- final norm -->
            <g data-tip="Final RMSNorm before the output projection: 2,048 params.">
              <rect class="sbox sbox-warm" x="120" y="390" width="320" height="36" rx="9"></rect>
              <text class="stitle" x="280" y="413" text-anchor="middle">final RMSNorm — 2,048 params</text>
            </g>
            <line class="flowline" x1="280" y1="426" x2="280" y2="440" marker-end="url(#arrS)"></line>

            <!-- LM head -->
            <g data-tip="Weight tying: the head is Eᵀ, so it adds zero new parameters. Output: one 151,936-way distribution per position — including every masked position at once.">
              <rect class="sbox" x="120" y="442" width="320" height="56" rx="10"></rect>
              <text class="stitle" x="280" y="464" text-anchor="middle">LM head — Eᵀ [2,048 × 151,936] (tied)</text>
              <text class="smono" x="280" y="486" text-anchor="middle">logits [L × 151,936]</text>
            </g>
            <line class="flowline" x1="280" y1="498" x2="280" y2="512" marker-end="url(#arrS)"></line>

            <!-- sampler -->
            <g data-tip="Not a weight — a loop. Each denoising pass commits the masked positions whose confidence clears a threshold; when the block is complete, its K/V are appended to the cache and the next block of masks opens.">
              <rect class="sbox sbox-accent" x="120" y="514" width="320" height="72" rx="12"></rect>
              <text class="stitle taccent" x="280" y="537" text-anchor="middle">block-diffusion decoding loop</text>
              <text class="ssub" x="280" y="556" text-anchor="middle">confidence-based unmasking inside the active block</text>
              <text class="ssub" x="280" y="573" text-anchor="middle">finalized block → K/V appended to cache</text>
            </g>

            <!-- feedback loop, left side -->
            <path class="loopline" d="M120,550 H52 Q40,550 40,538 V52 Q40,40 52,40 H110" marker-end="url(#arrSa)"></path>
            <text class="ssub taccent" x="28" y="300" transform="rotate(-90 28 300)" text-anchor="middle">committed tokens re-enter as context</text>

            <!-- right annotation -->
            <path d="M496,150 H488 V372 H496" fill="none" stroke="#d1cfc5" stroke-width="1.5"></path>
            <text class="anno" x="506" y="196">
              <tspan x="506" dy="0">Backbone = a standard dense</tspan>
              <tspan x="506" dy="17">decoder transformer — the same</tspan>
              <tspan x="506" dy="17">shape of weights an AR LM uses.</tspan>
              <tspan x="506" dy="17">SDAR initializes from Qwen3 and</tspan>
              <tspan x="506" dy="17">continues training with a block-</tspan>
              <tspan x="506" dy="17">diffusion objective; only the mask</tspan>
              <tspan x="506" dy="17">and the decoding loop change.</tspan>
            </text>

            <text class="smono" x="280" y="622" text-anchor="middle">28 layers × 50.33 M + 311.2 M embedding ≈ 1.72 B params ≈ 3.4 GB BF16</text>
          </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 2 · LAYER INTERNALS ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="layer-view">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h">2 · Inside one transformer block</h2>
        <p class="viz-sub">Left: the dataflow with every weight matrix and its shape. Right: the
          block-causal attention mask — hover a row to see exactly which K/V positions that query
          may read.</p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <div class="layer-grid">
            <!-- dataflow -->
            <div class="flow-col">
              <div class="sdar-scroll">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 460 960" role="img" aria-label="Transformer layer dataflow: RMSNorm, QKV projections with GQA, block-causal attention, output projection, SwiGLU MLP" style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:460px;">
                <defs>
                  <marker id="arrF" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6.5" markerHeight="6.5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#87857c"></path>
                  </marker>
                </defs>

                <!-- input -->
                <g data-tip="Hidden states entering the layer. At decode time L = cached context is NOT re-run; only the active block's positions flow through as queries.">
                  <rect class="sbox" x="110" y="20" width="240" height="44" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle" x="230" y="38" text-anchor="middle">X — hidden states</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="230" y="56" text-anchor="middle">[L × 2,048] BF16</text>
                </g>
                <line class="flowline" x1="230" y1="64" x2="230" y2="86" marker-end="url(#arrF)"></line>

                <!-- norm 1 -->
                <g data-tip="Pre-norm RMSNorm: 2,048 scale params. x / rms(x) · g">
                  <rect class="sbox sbox-warm" x="110" y="88" width="240" height="36" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle" x="230" y="111" text-anchor="middle">RMSNorm (2,048 params)</text>
                </g>

                <!-- branch to QKV -->
                <path class="flowline-thin" d="M230,124 V140 H76 V166" fill="none"></path>
                <line class="flowline-thin" x1="230" y1="140" x2="230" y2="166"></line>
                <path class="flowline-thin" d="M230,140 H384 V166" fill="none"></path>

                <g data-tip="W_Q: 2,048 × 2,048 = 4,194,304 params ≈ 8.4 MB BF16. Reshaped to 16 heads × 128 dims.">
                  <rect class="sbox" x="10" y="168" width="132" height="64" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle sm" x="76" y="188" text-anchor="middle">W_Q · 2048→2048</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="76" y="206" text-anchor="middle">16 heads × 128</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="76" y="222" text-anchor="middle">4.19 M</text>
                </g>
                <g data-tip="W_K: 2,048 × 1,024 = 2,097,152 params ≈ 4.2 MB BF16. GQA: only 8 KV heads.">
                  <rect class="sbox" x="164" y="168" width="132" height="64" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle sm" x="230" y="188" text-anchor="middle">W_K · 2048→1024</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="230" y="206" text-anchor="middle">8 KV heads × 128</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="230" y="222" text-anchor="middle">2.10 M</text>
                </g>
                <g data-tip="W_V: 2,048 × 1,024 = 2,097,152 params ≈ 4.2 MB BF16. K and V are what the cache stores.">
                  <rect class="sbox" x="318" y="168" width="132" height="64" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle sm" x="384" y="188" text-anchor="middle">W_V · 2048→1024</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="384" y="206" text-anchor="middle">8 KV heads × 128</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="384" y="222" text-anchor="middle">2.10 M</text>
                </g>

                <line class="flowline-thin" x1="76" y1="232" x2="76" y2="256"></line>
                <line class="flowline-thin" x1="230" y1="232" x2="230" y2="256"></line>

                <!-- qk norm + rope -->
                <g data-tip="Qwen3-style QK-norm: a per-head RMSNorm (128 params each for Q and K) before rotary position embedding.">
                  <rect class="sbox sbox-warm" x="10" y="258" width="286" height="30" rx="8"></rect>
                  <text class="ssub" x="153" y="278" text-anchor="middle">per-head RMSNorm on Q, K (dim 128) + RoPE</text>
                </g>

                <line class="flowline" x1="153" y1="288" x2="153" y2="314" marker-end="url(#arrF)"></line>
                <line class="flowline" x1="384" y1="232" x2="384" y2="314" marker-end="url(#arrF)"></line>

                <!-- attention -->
                <g data-tip="Scores are [16 heads × L_q × L_k] with mask M added before softmax. KV-cache cost: 2 (K,V) × 8 heads × 128 × 2 B = 4 KB per token per layer → 112 KB/token across 28 layers.">
                  <rect class="sbox sbox-accent" x="40" y="316" width="380" height="78" rx="11"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle taccent" x="230" y="339" text-anchor="middle">block-causal attention</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="230" y="359" text-anchor="middle">softmax(Q Kᵀ / √128 + M) V → [L × 16 × 128]</text>
                  <text class="ssub" x="230" y="378" text-anchor="middle">GQA: each K/V head serves 2 query heads · mask M → panel beside</text>
                </g>
                <line class="flowline" x1="230" y1="394" x2="230" y2="426" marker-end="url(#arrF)"></line>

                <!-- W_O -->
                <g data-tip="W_O: 2,048 × 2,048 = 4,194,304 params ≈ 8.4 MB BF16. Concatenates 16 × 128 head outputs back to d_model.">
                  <rect class="sbox" x="110" y="428" width="240" height="44" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle sm" x="230" y="446" text-anchor="middle">W_O — [2,048 × 2,048] · 4.19 M</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="230" y="464" text-anchor="middle">concat heads → 2,048</text>
                </g>
                <line class="flowline" x1="230" y1="472" x2="230" y2="491" marker-end="url(#arrF)"></line>

                <!-- residual 1 -->
                <path class="skipline" d="M110,42 H4 V506 H215" fill="none"></path>
                <circle class="rescirc" cx="230" cy="506" r="13"></circle>
                <text class="stitle" x="230" y="511" text-anchor="middle">+</text>
                <line class="flowline" x1="230" y1="519" x2="230" y2="542" marker-end="url(#arrF)"></line>

                <!-- norm 2 -->
                <g data-tip="Second pre-norm RMSNorm: 2,048 params.">
                  <rect class="sbox sbox-warm" x="110" y="544" width="240" height="36" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle" x="230" y="567" text-anchor="middle">RMSNorm (2,048 params)</text>
                </g>

                <!-- branch to gate/up -->
                <path class="flowline-thin" d="M230,580 V594 H118 V606" fill="none"></path>
                <path class="flowline-thin" d="M230,594 H342 V606" fill="none"></path>

                <g data-tip="W_gate: 2,048 × 6,144 = 12,582,912 params ≈ 25.2 MB BF16.">
                  <rect class="sbox" x="20" y="608" width="196" height="56" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle sm" x="118" y="630" text-anchor="middle">W_gate — [2,048 × 6,144]</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="118" y="650" text-anchor="middle">12.58 M</text>
                </g>
                <g data-tip="W_up: 2,048 × 6,144 = 12,582,912 params ≈ 25.2 MB BF16.">
                  <rect class="sbox" x="244" y="608" width="196" height="56" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle sm" x="342" y="630" text-anchor="middle">W_up — [2,048 × 6,144]</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="342" y="650" text-anchor="middle">12.58 M</text>
                </g>

                <line class="flowline-thin" x1="118" y1="664" x2="118" y2="698"></line>
                <line class="flowline-thin" x1="342" y1="664" x2="342" y2="698"></line>

                <g data-tip="SwiGLU nonlinearity: elementwise SiLU(gate) times up. No parameters here.">
                  <rect class="sbox sbox-warm" x="90" y="700" width="280" height="36" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="smono" x="230" y="723" text-anchor="middle">SiLU(gate) ⊙ up → [L × 6,144]</text>
                </g>
                <line class="flowline" x1="230" y1="736" x2="230" y2="766" marker-end="url(#arrF)"></line>

                <g data-tip="W_down: 6,144 × 2,048 = 12,582,912 params ≈ 25.2 MB BF16. MLP total: 37.75 M per layer — 3× the attention weights.">
                  <rect class="sbox" x="110" y="768" width="240" height="44" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle sm" x="230" y="786" text-anchor="middle">W_down — [6,144 × 2,048]</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="230" y="804" text-anchor="middle">12.58 M</text>
                </g>
                <line class="flowline" x1="230" y1="812" x2="230" y2="831" marker-end="url(#arrF)"></line>

                <!-- residual 2 -->
                <path class="skipline" d="M230,532 H8 V846 H215" fill="none"></path>
                <circle class="rescirc" cx="230" cy="846" r="13"></circle>
                <text class="stitle" x="230" y="851" text-anchor="middle">+</text>
                <line class="flowline" x1="230" y1="859" x2="230" y2="882" marker-end="url(#arrF)"></line>

                <!-- output -->
                <g data-tip="Same shape out as in — 28 of these blocks are stacked.">
                  <rect class="sbox" x="110" y="884" width="240" height="44" rx="9"></rect>
                  <text class="stitle" x="230" y="902" text-anchor="middle">X′ — [L × 2,048]</text>
                  <text class="smono" x="230" y="920" text-anchor="middle">→ layer ℓ+1</text>
                </g>

                <text class="smono" x="230" y="952" text-anchor="middle">one layer ≈ 50.33 M params · × 28 = 1.41 B · + 311 M embedding ≈ 1.72 B</text>
              </svg>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- mask panel -->
            <div class="mask-col">
              <div class="mask-modes">
                <button class="mode-btn on" id="modeTrain" type="button">Training view — all queries</button>
                <button class="mode-btn" id="modeDec" type="button">Decoding view — active block B2</button>
              </div>

              <div class="mask-wrap" id="maskWrap">
                <svg id="maskSvg" viewBox="0 0 470 460" role="img" aria-label="Block-causal attention mask: 12 positions in 3 blocks of 4; bidirectional within a block, causal across blocks" style="width:100%; max-width:480px; height:auto; display:block; margin:0 auto;">
                  <text class="stitle sm" x="117" y="16" text-anchor="middle">B0 · t0–t3</text>
                  <text class="stitle sm" x="245" y="16" text-anchor="middle">B1 · t4–t7</text>
                  <text class="stitle sm taccent" x="373" y="16" text-anchor="middle">B2 · t8–t11</text>
                  <rect x="54" y="22" width="126" height="3" rx="1.5" fill="#d4a27f"></rect>
                  <rect x="182" y="22" width="126" height="3" rx="1.5" fill="#d4a27f"></rect>
                  <rect x="310" y="22" width="126" height="3" rx="1.5" fill="#d97757"></rect>

                  {maskRows[0].cells.map((c) => (
                    <text class="mlabel" x={54 + c.k * 32 + 15} y="52" text-anchor="middle">t{c.k}</text>
                  ))}

                  {maskRows.map((row) => (
                    <g class={`mrow ${row.q < 8 ? 'row-prev' : 'row-cur'}`} data-q={row.q}>
                      <text class="mlabel" x="46" y={64 + row.q * 32 + 19} text-anchor="end">t{row.q}</text>
                      {row.cells.map((c) => (
                        <rect class={`mcell ${c.cls}`} x={54 + c.k * 32} y={64 + row.q * 32} width="30" height="30" rx="4"></rect>
                      ))}
                      <rect class="mhit" x="4" y={64 + row.q * 32} width="460" height="32"></rect>
                    </g>
                  ))}

                  <line class="mdiag" x1="54" y1="64" x2="438" y2="448"></line>
                </svg>
              </div>

              <div class="mask-legend">
                <span><i class="sw sw-past"></i> earlier block — causal, K/V read from cache</span>
                <span><i class="sw sw-intra"></i> same block — bidirectional (future visible)</span>
                <span><i class="sw sw-off"></i> later block — masked out</span>
                <span><i class="sw sw-diag"></i> strict AR causal boundary, for comparison</span>
              </div>

              <p class="mask-caption" id="maskCaption">Hover a row: each row is one query position;
                filled cells are the K/V positions it may attend to. Coral cells right of the dashed
                diagonal are exactly what block diffusion adds over an AR mask.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 3 · DECODING TIMELINE ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="decode-view">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h">3 · Decoding timeline</h2>
        <p class="viz-sub">Step through block-by-block generation: masked slots are denoised in
          parallel, commits follow confidence, and each finalized block appends exact K/V entries
          to the cache.</p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <div class="dt-controls">
            <button class="btn ghost btn-sm" id="btnReset" type="button">⟲ Reset</button>
            <button class="btn ghost btn-sm" id="btnPrev" type="button">← Prev</button>
            <button class="btn btn-sm" id="btnNext" type="button">Next →</button>
            <button class="btn ghost btn-sm" id="btnPlay" type="button">▶ Play</button>
            <span class="dt-step" id="dtStep">Step 0 / 10 — Prefill</span>
          </div>

          <div class="dt-strip" id="dtStrip">
            <span class="blk prompt-blk">
              <span class="blk-label">prompt · in KV cache</span>
              <span class="blk-toks">
                <span class="chip p">The</span><span class="chip p">capital</span><span class="chip p">of</span><span class="chip p">France</span><span class="chip p">is</span>
              </span>
            </span>
          </div>

          <p class="dt-caption" id="dtCaption">Prefill — the 5-token prompt runs through all 28
            layers once. Every layer writes K and V for the 5 positions: 5 × 112 KB = 560 KB of
            cache. Identical to an AR model so far.</p>

          <div class="dt-meters" id="dtMeters">forward passes 1 (1 prefill + 0 denoise) · tokens committed 0 · AR passes for the same tokens: 0</div>

          <div class="cache-panel">
            <div class="cache-title">KV cache — 28 layers × 8 KV heads × 128 dims × 2 (K,V) × BF16 = <b>112 KB / token</b></div>
            <div class="cache-row" id="dtCache">
              <span class="cc g-p"></span><span class="cc g-p"></span><span class="cc g-p"></span><span class="cc g-p"></span><span class="cc g-p"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="cache-label" id="dtCacheLbl">5 tokens × 112 KB = 560 KB</div>
          </div>

          <noscript>
            <p class="viz-sub">This explorer steps through 10 decoding states with JavaScript
              enabled; without it you are seeing the initial prefill state.</p>
          </noscript>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ PROSE ============ -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="prose">
          <h2>Reading the diagram</h2>

          <h3>Stage 1 — the stack is just a transformer</h3>
          <p>
            There is no diffusion-specific machinery in the weights. The stack is a plain dense
            decoder: a 151,936 × 2,048 tied embedding (311 M parameters), 28 identical transformer
            blocks of about 50.3 M parameters each, a final RMSNorm, and the transposed embedding
            as the LM head — roughly 1.72 B parameters, 3.4 GB in BF16. This is why SDAR-style
            models can be <em>adapted</em> from a pretrained AR checkpoint rather than trained
            from scratch: the published recipe starts from Qwen3 weights and continues training
            with a block-diffusion objective. Everything that makes the model “diffusion” lives
            in two places outside the weights: the attention mask and the decoding loop.
          </p>

          <h3>Stage 2 — one layer, and the mask that changes everything</h3>
          <p>
            Inside a block: pre-RMSNorm, then Q/K/V projections. The config is GQA-shaped —
            16 query heads of dimension 128 (W<sub>Q</sub>: 2,048 → 2,048) but only 8 KV heads
            (W<sub>K</sub>, W<sub>V</sub>: 2,048 → 1,024), so each K/V head serves two query
            heads and the cache is half the size it would be with MHA. After per-head QK-norm and
            RoPE comes the one genuinely different ingredient: the <strong>block-causal mask</strong>.
            Partition positions into blocks of 4. A query may attend to every position in earlier
            blocks (ordinary causal attention — those K/V come straight from the cache) and to
            <em>every</em> position of its own block, including future ones. In the matrix panel,
            the coral cells to the right of the dashed diagonal are precisely the visibility that
            a causal AR mask forbids — and they are what lets several tokens be predicted jointly
            in one pass. The MLP is a standard SwiGLU (2,048 → 6,144 → 2,048, 37.75 M parameters
            per layer — three times the attention weights).
          </p>

          <h3>Stage 3 — decode in blocks, cache like an AR model</h3>
          <p>
            Generation appends a block of 4 <code>[MASK]</code> tokens and denoises it over a few
            forward passes. Each pass produces a full 151,936-way distribution at every masked
            position simultaneously; positions whose confidence clears a threshold τ are committed
            (at least the argmax is, so progress is guaranteed), and committed tokens condition the
            next pass. Commit order follows confidence, not left-to-right position. In the timeline
            above, 8 tokens land in 5 denoising passes instead of 8 AR steps. When a block is
            finished it is frozen; because cross-block attention is causal, its K and V are
            <em>exact</em> — bit-for-bit what an AR pass would have produced — so they are appended
            to the cache once and never touched again. The cache simply grows in block-sized
            strides: 112 KB per token in this config.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="eff-note band-dark">
          <h3>Why this matters for efficiency</h3>
          <p>
            Two separate levers hide in this design. <strong>Within-block parallelism attacks the
            weight-read floor.</strong> Batch-1 decoding is memory-bound: every forward pass streams
            all ≈3.4 GB of weights through the GPU regardless of how many tokens it commits, so a
            pass that commits 2–3 tokens cuts the weight traffic <em>per token</em> by 2–3×. The
            tokens-per-pass ratio, controlled by the confidence threshold and block size, is nearly
            free throughput. <strong>Block-causality makes KV reuse exact.</strong> Full-attention
            diffusion LMs let every position keep revising, so any cached K/V can go stale and
            cache reuse becomes an approximation to manage. Here, finalized blocks are immutable by
            construction — the cache is append-only and exact, the same contract an AR engine
            relies on. The trade lives between the two levers: larger blocks buy more parallelism
            but weaken left-to-right conditioning inside the block; the released SDAR checkpoints
            settle at a short block length of 4.
          </p>
          <div class="eff-chips">
            <span class="eff-chip">1 fwd pass ≈ 3.4 GB weight reads (BF16, batch 1)</span>
            <span class="eff-chip">KV: 112 KB/token — exact, append-only</span>
            <span class="eff-chip">tokens/pass &gt; 1 is the whole game</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="prose">
          <h2>Going deeper</h2>
          <ul class="deeper-list">
            <li><a class="arrow-link" href="https://github.com/JetAstra/SDAR" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SDAR — model family, checkpoints &amp; tech report (GitHub)</a></li>
            <li><a class="arrow-link" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.09573" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Block Diffusion (BD3-LM) — interpolating between AR and diffusion LMs</a></li>
            <li><a class="arrow-link" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.09992" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LLaDA — large language diffusion models (full-attention dLLM)</a></li>
            <li><a class="arrow-link" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.22618" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Fast-dLLM — KV caching &amp; parallel decoding for diffusion LLMs</a></li>
            <li><a class="arrow-link" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.09388" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Qwen3 technical report — the backbone family</a></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="fine-print">
            Shapes on this page assume the public SDAR-1.7B configuration (Qwen3-1.7B backbone:
            d = 2,048, 28 layers, 16 Q / 8 KV heads, head_dim 128, FFN 6,144, vocab 151,936,
            block length 4). The larger released variants (4B, 8B, and the 30B-A3B MoE) change
            widths and depths, not the mechanics shown here. Confidence numbers in the timeline
            are illustrative.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div id="sdarTip" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
</Base>

